t as the current code does","when":"formatCitation is called with that citation"},{"given":"the same citation as AC-1 (YouTube, video_url 'not-a-url', snippet 'Relevant text', 10–20 s range)","id":"AC-2","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation","then":"the returned string starts with `- ` and still contains the exact fragment `(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20` — this fragment is the deferred-red expected_symptom the current code emits (title + unavailable note + range with em-dash U+2014 and en-dash U+2013), so on the unchanged tree the failing assertion prints it in the received value; the new `- ` prefix and snippet line are what turn it green","when":"formatCitation is called with that citation"},{"given":"a citation with source_type 'dynamous', an empty lesson_url, a video_title, and a non-empty snippet (e.g. the base fixture's 'Test snippet text')","id":"AC-3","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation","then":"the returned string starts with `- `, contains no `](` anywhere (still no markdown link), and still contains its `> \"<snippet>\"` blockquote on its own line","when":"formatCitation is called with that citation"},{"given":"a default-source (YouTube) citation whose video_url parses but has no `v` parameter (e.g. 'https://www.youtube.com/'), a non-empty snippet, and the 10–20 s range","id":"AC-4","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation","then":"the returned string starts with `- `, still contains the fragment `(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20` (no `[title](url)` markdown link around the title), and contains the `> \"<snippet>\"` blockquote on its own line — the same shape as the unparseable-URL fallback, since the issue Background names both branches as the same defect","when":"formatCitation is called with that citation"}],"dependencies":[],"invariants":["Every existing case in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts keeps passing unchanged; sharpest pins: the exact console.warn message '[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \"<url>\"' still fires on both YouTube fallback branches, the invalid-URL fallback still does not wrap the title in a markdown link (not.toContain('[Test Video Title](')), the Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback still contains no '](', and empty/blank/undefined snippet still returns ''.","The fix covers both YouTube fallback branches — the URL constructor throwing and the URL parsing but yielding no `v` parameter — with identical output shape; the issue Background explicitly names both.","After the fix, no formatCitation path that returns a non-empty string may omit the '- ' list marker or the blockquote snippet line; every path shares the shape '- ' + (markdown link, or plain title text when no link exists) + ' — ' + range + newline + two-space-indented '> \"snippet\"'.","Valid-path output is frozen: the valid YouTube deep-link string, the valid Dynamous lesson_url string, formatTimestamp's output, the formatSources header/join, the export header, and the filename slug must not change.","Only production file changed: app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts; test changes confined to app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts; no new or changed dependencies; no backend, schema, api.ts, or component changes.","Unicode bytes preserved: em-dash U+2014 between title/link and range (in the output and inside the console.warn message), en-dash U+2013 inside timestamp ranges — existing assertions and the deferred-red symptom match on these exact characters."],"issue":{"number":49,"title":"fix(export): markdown export drops the transcript snippet when a citation URL cannot be parsed"},"out_of_scope":["Backend, database schema, dependencies, CitationModal.tsx, Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, Sidebar.tsx (issue out-of-scope list).","The valid-URL YouTube path and the valid-lesson_url Dynamous path, formatTimestamp, the export header and the filename slug (issue out-of-scope list).","formatSources, exportConversationAsMarkdown, and src/lib/api.ts — the Citation type already carries source_type/lesson_url; the empty/blank-snippet early return of '' also stays as-is.","Nearby oddities noted by the investigation: blank lines in exports when a snippet is empty, the duplicated console.warn blocks, and the brittle split('- [Test Video]') count assertion — none are fixed in this PR."],"risks":["The existing formatSources multi-citation test counts occurrences via split('- [Test Video]'); any accidental change to valid-path output breaks it — keep the change confined to the three fallback return statements.","The console.warn message is pinned byte-exactly by an existing test (em-dash included); unifying the two duplicated warn blocks is allowed only if the emitted message stays identical.","Adding the blockquote to the YouTube fallbacks must not introduce a markdown link — the existing not.toContain('[Test Video Title](') assertion still applies — and must not disturb the em/en-dash bytes the existing assertions match.","Acceptance fixtures must use the 10–20 s range so the fragment '0:10–0:20' and the deferred-red symptom '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' are byte-identical to the issue's quoted output; any other second values change the expected string.","The marker addition changes rendered markdown for fallback entries from 'merges into the previous list item' to 'own list item' — that is the intended fix; do not compensate by stripping the '- ' marker on any other path."],"summary":"Repair the three fallback branches of formatCitation in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts so every emitted citation line follows the complete-path convention: leading `- ` list marker, ` — ` + timestamp range, then a newline + two-space-indented `> \"<snippet>\"` blockquote line. Both YouTube fallbacks (video_url unparseable, or parseable with no `v` parameter) keep title, `(timestamp link unavailable)` and the range but regain the snippet blockquote and the `- ` marker they currently drop; the Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback keeps its snippet and regains the `- ` marker. Valid-path output is unchanged.","version":"2.0"},"sha256":"ad3623538793ca23ee13c051faea289a7928fc4736e3786f3f4a4045f13b34e1","source":"task-contract.json"},"design":{"content":{"ac_mapping":{"AC-1":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-2":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-3":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-4":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"]},"allowed_new_files":[],"context_sha256":"9f52c5370e776c91cd372763468b8f5a0baae1a9686561d4eb08762a94eb0f83","contract_sha256":"ad3623538793ca23ee13c051faea289a7928fc4736e3786f3f4a4045f13b34e1","data_flows":["Citation -> formatCitation -> markdown list item ('- ' + [title](url) or plain title + em-dash + m:ss range pair + newline + two-space-indented '> \"snippet\"'), or '' when snippet is empty/blank","Message.sources -> formatSources -> '**Sources:**' header + newline-joined formatCitation lines","conversation + messages -> exportConversationAsMarkdown -> Blob -> saveAs download"],"invariants":["Every formatCitation path returning a non-empty string emits the complete shape: '- ' + (markdown link, or plain title text when no link exists) + em-dash U+2014 + range (en-dash U+2013 inside) + newline + two-space-indented '> \"<snippet>\"'.","Empty/blank/undefined snippet still returns '' via the unchanged early return.","console.warn '[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link - invalid video_url: \"<url>\"' (byte-exact, em-dash U+2014 included) still fires on both YouTube fallback branches; the duplicated warn blocks stay as-is.","YouTube fallback entries still contain no '[Test Video Title](' markdown link; Dynamous empty-lesson_url entries still contain no ']('.","Valid-path output frozen: valid YouTube deep-link string, valid Dynamous lesson_url string, formatTimestamp output, formatSources header/join, export header, filename slug.","Every existing case in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts keeps passing unchanged; Unicode bytes (em-dash U+2014, en-dash U+2013) preserved in output and assertions."],"modules":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts"],"planned_files":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts","app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts"],"public_interfaces":["formatCitation(citation: Citation) -> string"],"seams":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"version":"1.0"},"sha256":"f0b081346b6f01606ffc9785596fbd84c9e17ea11c15a6f9bb3c74c723c10982","source":"design.json"},"frontier":{"content":{"accepted":true,"blockers":[],"issue":49,"ready":true,"ticket_sha256":"bb99dc8e6d970c10fef7233713b22bd8cad3ee43f1f83001b531e50ff80aa90a","version":"1.0"},"sha256":"f7fadc6183364b564359e5a36ef32067b4a76ec18a228f53f6e909297edc809b","source":"frontier.json"},"green-proof":{"content":{"architecture_builder":{"changed_files":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts","app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts"],"context_sha256":"9f52c5370e776c91cd372763468b8f5a0baae1a9686561d4eb08762a94eb0f83","contract_sha256":"ad3623538793ca23ee13c051faea289a7928fc4736e3786f3f4a4045f13b34e1","convergence":"improves","debts":[],"design_sha256":"f0b081346b6f01606ffc9785596fbd84c9e17ea11c15a6f9bb3c74c723c10982","diff_sha256":"550c069eb51e9a55b821932427fa149da8ee302ec293952750b3bf12fb5c53e9","findings":[],"governor_sha256":"9869393cb018673feb18ab6019b5e8f549dcc818e43bd314b62fbd2de380f429","head_sha":"65721af95e50209e02e625b148af43a38a3d8b52","migrations":[],"policy_sha256":"0db30c9f1e05383df234c84feb31dcef348f09ec605db423606b9f72c7e54add","principles":["ARCH-DEEP-MODULES","ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES"],"rationale":["The diff touches exactly app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts and its co-located exportMarkdown.test.ts, matching the planned_files envelope with no new files, no dependency changes, and no backend or component changes.","ARCH-DEEP-MODULES conform: the repair edits the thr